== Chapter VII

#block(inset: (x: 1em))[
  #set par(justify: false)
  #text(size: 0.9em)[#emph[General Rules, without which no Lust will be mortified. No Mortification unless a man be a Believer. Dangers of attempting Mortification of Sin by Unregenerate Persons. The Duty of unconverted Persons, as to this business of Mortification, considered. The vanity of the Papists Attempts, and Rules for Mortification thence discovered.]]
]

=== II. General Rules

#smallcaps[THE] #emph[ways] and Means whereby a Soul may proceed to the #emph[Mortification] of any particular #emph[lust] and Sin, which Satan takes Advantage by, to disquiet and weaken him, comes next under Consideration.

Now there are some #emph[General Considerations] to be premised, concerning some Principles and Foundations of this work, without which #emph[no man] in the world, be he never so much raised by #emph[Convictions,] and resolved for the Mortification of any Sin, can attain thereunto.

General #emph[Rules] and Principles, without which no Sin will be ever mortified, are these,

==== First Rule: Only a Believer Can Mortify Sin

1\. Unless a Man be a #emph[Believer,] that is, one that is truly #emph[ingrafted] into Christ, he can never mortify any one Sin; I do not say, unless he #emph[know] himself to be so, but unless #emph[indeed] he be so. Mortification is the work of #emph[Believers,] Rom 8:13. #emph[If ye through the Spirit] etc. #emph[Ye Believers,] to whom there is no #emph[condemnation,] v. 1. They alone are exhorted to it. Col 3:5. #emph[Mortify therefore your members that are upon the earth.] Who should #emph[mortify?] You who #emph[are risen with Christ,] v. 1 whose #emph[Life is hid with Christ] in God, v. 3 who shall #emph[appear with him in Glory,] v. 4. An #emph[unregenerate] man may do something like it, but the work itself, so as it may be #emph[acceptable] with God, he can never perform. You know what a Picture of it is drawn in some of the #emph[Philosophers, Seneca, Tully, Epictetus]\; what affectionate Discourses they have of #emph[contempt] of the World, and Self, of #emph[regulating] and #emph[conquering] all #emph[exorbitant] Affections and Passions. The Lives of most of them manifested, that their #emph[Maxims] differed as much from true Mortification, as the #emph[Sun] painted on a #emph[Sign-post,] from the #emph[Sun] in the #emph[Firmament.] They had neither Light nor Heat. Their own #emph[Lucian] sufficiently manifests what they #emph[all] were. There is no Death of Sin, without the #emph[Death] of Christ. You know what Attempts there are made after it by the #emph[Papists,] in their #emph[Vows, Penances,] and #emph[Satisfactions]\; I dare say of Them (I mean as many of them as act upon the Principles of their Church, as they #emph[call it,]) what #emph[Paul] says of #emph[Israel] in point of #emph[Righteousness,] Rom 9:31, 32. They have #emph[followed after Mortification,] but they have not Attained to it; Wherefore? Because they #emph[seek it not by Faith, but as it were by the works of the Law.] The same is the State and Condition of all amongst ourselves, who in Obedience to their Convictions, and #emph[awakened] Consciences, do attempt a Relinquishment of Sin; they follow #emph[after] it, but they do not Attain it.

It is true, it #emph[is,] it #emph[will] be required of every person whatever, that hears the #emph[Law] or #emph[Gospel] preached, that he #emph[mortify Sin]\; It is his #emph[Duty,] but it is not his #emph[immediate] Duty; It is his #emph[Duty] to do it, but to do it in Gods way. If you require your Servant to pay so much Money for you in such a place, but first to go and take it up in another; it is his Duty to pay the Money appointed, and you will #emph[blame] him if he do it not; yet it was not his #emph[immediate] Duty; he was first to #emph[take it up,] according to your #emph[direction.] So it is in this Case; Sin is to be #emph[mortified,] but something is to be done in the #emph[first place] to enable us thereunto.

I have #emph[proved,] that it is the #emph[Spirit] alone that can #emph[mortify] Sin; He is #emph[promised] to do it, and all other #emph[means] without him are #emph[empty] and vain. How shall he then #emph[mortify] Sin, that hath not the #emph[Spirit]? A man may easier #emph[see] without #emph[Eyes,] speak without a #emph[Tongue,] than truly #emph[Mortify] one Sin without the Spirit. Now how is he attained? It is the #emph[Spirit] of Christ; and (as the Apostle says,) if we #emph[have not the Spirit of Christ, we are none of his,] Rom 8:9. So, if we are #emph[Christs,] have an #emph[Interest] in him, we have the #emph[Spirit,] and so alone have power for Mortification. This the Apostle discourses at large, Rom 8:8. #emph[So then they that are in the flesh cannot please God.] It is the Inference and Conclusion he makes of his foregoing Discourse about our #emph[Natural] state and Condition, and the #emph[Enmity] we have unto God and his #emph[Law] therein. If we are in the #emph[flesh,] if we have not the #emph[Spirit,] we #emph[cannot] do any thing that should please God. But what is our deliverance from this Condition, v. 9. #emph[But ye are not in the flesh, but in the Spirit, if so be that the Spirit of God dwell in you:] Ye Believers, that have the #emph[Spirit of Christ,] ye are not in the #emph[flesh.] There is no way of Deliverance from the State and Condition of #emph[being in the flesh,] but by the #emph[Spirit] of #emph[Christ]\; And what if this Spirit of Christ be in you? Why then you are #emph[mortified,] v. 10 the Body is #emph[dead because of Sin,] or unto it; Mortification is carried on; the New Man is #emph[quickened] to Righteousness. This the Apostle proves v. 11 from the #emph[Union] we have with Christ by the #emph[Spirit,] which will produce #emph[suitable Operations] in us, to what it wrought in him. All #emph[attempts] then for Mortification of any Lust, without an Interest in Christ, are #emph[vain.] Many men that are #emph[galled] with and for #emph[Sin,] (the #emph[arrows] of Christ for #emph[Conviction] by the Preaching of the Word, or some Affliction having been made #emph[sharp] in their hearts) do #emph[vigorously] set themselves against this or that particular #emph[Lust,] wherewith their Consciences have been most #emph[disquieted] or #emph[perplexed.] But poor Creatures! They labor in the Fire, and their #emph[work] consumeth. When the #emph[Spirit] of Christ comes to this work, he will be as #emph[Refiners Fire,] and as #emph[Fullers] Soap, and he will purge men as #emph[Gold] and #emph[Silver,] Mal 3:3 take away their #emph[dross] and #emph[tin,] their #emph[filth] and #emph[blood,] as Isa 4:4. But men must be #emph[Gold] and #emph[Silver] in the bottom, or else Refining will do them no good. The #emph[Prophet] gives us the #emph[sad] issue of #emph[wicked] men's utmost Attempts for #emph[Mortification,] by what Means soever that God #emph[affords] them, Jer 6:29, 30. #emph[The Bellows are burnt, and the Lead is consumed of the fire, the Founder melteth in vain, Reprobate Silver shall men call them, because the Lord hath rejected them]\; And what is the Reason hereof? v. 28 they were #emph[Brass] and #emph[Iron] when they were put into the Furnace. Men may refine #emph[Brass] and #emph[Iron] long enough before they will be good #emph[Silver.]

I say then, #emph[Mortification] is not the #emph[present] business of #emph[unregenerate] men. God calls them not to it as #emph[yet. Conversion] is their work. The #emph[Conversion] of the #emph[whole] Soul, not the #emph[Mortification] of #emph[this] or #emph[that particular] Lust. You would #emph[laugh] at a man, that you should see setting up a #emph[great Fabric,] and never take any care for a #emph[Foundation]\; especially if you should #emph[see] him so #emph[foolish,] as that having a #emph[thousand] Experiences, that what he built one day, fell down another, he would yet continue in the same course. So it is with convinced Persons; Though they plainly see, that what #emph[ground] they get against Sin #emph[one] day, they lose #emph[another,] yet they will go on in the same Road still, without inquiring where the #emph[destructive flaw] in their progress lies. When the #emph[Jews] upon the #emph[Conviction] of their Sin were #emph[cut to the heart,] Acts 2:37 and cried out #emph[what shall we do?] What doth #emph[Peter] direct them to? Does he bid them #emph[go] and #emph[mortify] their #emph[pride, wrath, malice, cruelty,] and the like? No, he knew that was not their #emph[present] work, but he calls them to #emph[Conversion] and #emph[Faith] in Christ in General, v. 38. Let the Soul be first thoroughly #emph[converted,] and then #emph[looking] on him whom they had pierced, #emph[Humiliation] and Mortification will ensue. Thus when #emph[John] came to preach #emph[Repentance] and #emph[Conversion,] he said, The #emph[Axe] is now #emph[laid to the root of the tree,] Matt 3:10. The #emph[Pharisees] had been laying #emph[heavy] Burdens, imposing #emph[tedious] Duties, and rigid means of Mortification, in #emph[Fastings, Washings,] and the like, all in vain: Says #emph[John,] The #emph[Doctrine of Conversion] is for you, the #emph[axe] in my hand is laid to the #emph[root.] And our Savior tells us what is to be done in this #emph[case]\; says he, Do men gather #emph[Grapes] from #emph[Thorns?] Matt 7:16. But suppose a #emph[Thorn] be well #emph[pruned] and cut, and have pains taken with #emph[him?] Yea but he will never #emph[bear Figs]\; vv. 17, 18. It cannot be but every Tree will bring forth Fruit according to its own #emph[kind.] What is then to be done, he tells us, Matt 12:33. #emph[Make the Tree Good, and his Fruit will be good:] The #emph[Root] must be dealt with, the Nature of the #emph[Tree] changed, or no good Fruit will be brought forth.

This is that I aim at, unless a man be #emph[Regenerate,] unless he be a #emph[Believer,] all Attempts that he can make for #emph[Mortification,] be they never so #emph[specious] and promising, all Means he can use, let him follow them with never so much Diligence, Earnestness, Watchfulness and Contention of Mind and Spirit, are to no purpose; In vain shall he use many #emph[remedies,] he shall #emph[not be healed.] Yea there are #emph[sundry desperate] Evils attending an Endeavor in #emph[convinced] Persons that are no more but so, to perform this #emph[Duty.]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[First, The #emph[mind] and Soul is taken #emph[up] about that which is not the mans #emph[proper business,] and so He is diverted from that which is so. God lays hold by his #emph[Word] and #emph[Judgments] on some #emph[Sin] in him, galls his #emph[Conscience,] disquiets his #emph[heart,] deprives him of his #emph[Rest]\; now #emph[other] Diversions will not serve his #emph[turn]: He must apply himself to the #emph[work] before him. The business in hand being to awake the whole Man unto a consideration of the State and Condition wherein he #emph[is,] that he might be brought #emph[home] to God; instead hereof, he sets himself to #emph[mortify] the Sin that #emph[galls] him; which is a pure #emph[issue] of Self-love, to be freed from his #emph[trouble]\; and not at all to the #emph[work he is called] unto; and so is #emph[diverted] from it. Thus God tells us of #emph[Ephraim,] when he #emph[spread] his #emph[Net] upon them, and brought #emph[them] down as the #emph[Fowls] of Heaven, and #emph[chastised] them, Hos 7:12. #emph[caught] them, #emph[entangled] them, #emph[convinced] them, that they could not escape; saith he of them, #emph[They return, but not to the most High:] They set themselves to a #emph[Relinquishment] of Sin, but not in that manner by universal #emph[conversion] as #emph[God] called for it. Thus are men #emph[diverted] from coming unto God, by the most #emph[glorious] ways that they can fix upon to come to him by. And this is one of the most common #emph[deceits] whereby men ruin their own Souls; I wish that some whose Trade it is to #emph[daub with untempered Mortar] in the things of God, did not teach this Deceit, and cause the People to err by their Ignorance: What do men do? What oft-times are they directed #emph[unto,] when their Consciences are galled by Sin, and Disquietment from the Lord hath laid hold upon them? Is not a Relinquishment of the Sin as to Practice, (that they are in some Fruits of it perplexed withal, and making head against it,) the sum of what they apply themselves unto? And is not the Gospel End of their Convictions lost thereby? Here men abide and perish.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[Secondly, This #emph[Duty] being a thing good in itself, in its proper place, a Duty evidencing #emph[Sincerity,] bringing home #emph[Peace] to the Conscience; a man finding himself #emph[really] engaged in it, his Mind and Heart set against this or that Sin, with #emph[purpose] and Resolution to have no more to #emph[do] with it, he is ready to #emph[conclude,] that his #emph[state] and Condition is #emph[good,] and so to delude his #emph[own] Soul. For,]]

#pad(left: 4.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[(1.) When his #emph[Conscience] hath been made sick with Sin, and he could find no rest, when he should go to the #emph[great] Physician of Souls, and get #emph[healing] in his Blood; the Man by this Engagement against Sin, pacifies and quiets his Conscience, and sits down without going to Christ at all. Ah! how many #emph[poor Souls] are thus #emph[deluded] to Eternity! When #emph[Ephraim saw his sickness, he sent to King Jareb,] Hos 5:13 which kept him off from God. The whole bundle of the Popish Religion is made up of Designs and #emph[contrivances] to pacify Conscience without Christ; all #emph[described] by the Apostle, Rom 10:4.]]

#pad(left: 4.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[(2.) By this means men #emph[satisfy] themselves that their State and Condition is #emph[good,] seeing they do that which is a work good in itself, and they do not do it to be #emph[seen.] They know they would have the work done in #emph[sincerity,] and so are #emph[hardened] in a kind of #emph[self] Righteousness.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[(3.) When a man hath thus for a #emph[season] been #emph[deluded,] and hath #emph[deceived] his own Soul, and finds in a #emph[long course] of Life, that indeed his sin is not #emph[mortified,] or if he hath changed one, he hath gotten another; He begins at #emph[length] to think, that all #emph[contending] is in #emph[vain,] he shall never be able to prevail: He is making a #emph[Dam] against #emph[Water] that increaseth on him Hereupon he gives #emph[over,] as one despairing of #emph[any] success, and yields up himself to the #emph[power] of sin, and that #emph[habit] of #emph[Formality] that he hath gotten.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[And this is the usual Issue with Persons attempting the #emph[Mortification] of sin without an #emph[Interest] in Christ first obtained. It #emph[deludes] them, #emph[hardens] them, #emph[destroys] them. And therefore we see that there are not usually more vile and desperate sinners in the world, than such as having by #emph[Conviction] been put on this Course have found it fruitless, and deserted it without a discovery of Christ. And this is the substance of the Religion and Godliness of the choicest #emph[Formalists] in the world; and of all those who in the #emph[Roman] Synagogue are drawn to #emph[Mortification] as they drive #emph[Indians] to Baptism, or #emph[Cattle] to water. I say then that Mortification is the work of #emph[Believers,] and Believers only. To #emph[kill] sin is the work of #emph[living] men; where men are #emph[dead,] (as all Unbelievers, the #emph[best] of them are #emph[dead,]) sin is #emph[alive,] and will #emph[live.]]]

#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[2\. It is the work of #emph[Faith]\; the #emph[peculiar] work of Faith; Now if there be a #emph[work] to be done that will be effected by #emph[one] only #emph[instrument,] it is the greatest #emph[madness] for any to attempt the doing of it, that hath not that Instrument. Now it is Faith that #emph[purifies the Heart,] Acts 15:9 or as #emph[Peter] speaks, #emph[we purify our Souls in obeying the Truth through the Spirit,] 1 Pet 1:22. And without it, it will not be done.]

What hath been spoken, I suppose is sufficient to make good my first #emph[general Rule: Be sure to get an Interest in Christ, if you intend to mortify any sin, without it it will never be done.]

#emph[Ob.] You will say, What then would you have #emph[unregenerate] men, that are convinced of the Evil of sin do? Shall they cease #emph[striving] against #emph[sin,] live #emph[dissolutely,] give their Lusts their #emph[swinge,] and be as bad as the worst of men? This were a way to set the whole world into Confusion, to bring all things into darkness, to set open the #emph[flood-gates] of #emph[lust,] and lay the Reins upon the #emph[Necks] of men to #emph[rush] into all sin with delight and greediness, like the #emph[horse] into the battle.

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[#emph[Ans.] 1. God forbid! It is to be looked on as a great issue of the Wisdom, Goodness, and Love of God, that by manifold ways and means he is pleased to restrain the Sons of men from running forth into that compass of #emph[excess] and #emph[riot,] which the #emph[depravedness] of their Nature would carry them out unto with #emph[violence.] By what way soever this is done, it is an issue of the #emph[care, kindness,] and #emph[Goodness] of God, without which the whole Earth would be an #emph[Hell] of Sin and Confusion.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[2\. There is a peculiar #emph[convincing] Power in the Word, which God is often-times pleased to #emph[put forth] to the wounding, #emph[amazing,] and in some sort humbling of Sinners, though they are never converted. And the Word is to be #emph[preached, though] it hath #emph[this] End, yet not #emph[with] this End. Let then the Word be preached, and the #emph[sins] of men rebuked, #emph[Lust] will be #emph[restrained,] and some Oppositions will be made against Sin, though that be not the #emph[Effect] aimed at.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[3\. Though this be the #emph[work] of the Word and Spirit, and it be good in itself, yet it is not profitable nor available as to the main End in them in whom it is wrought; they are still in the #emph[gall of Bitterness,] and under the #emph[power] of darkness.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[4\. Let men know it is their #emph[Duty,] but in its proper place; I take not men from #emph[Mortification,] but put them upon #emph[Conversion.] He that shall call a man from #emph[mending] a #emph[Hole] in the Wall of his #emph[House,] to #emph[quench a Fire] that is consuming the whole #emph[Building,] is not his Enemy. Poor Soul! It is not thy #emph[Sore-finger] but thy #emph[Hectic-Fever] that thou art to #emph[apply] thyself to the Consideration of. Thou settest thyself against a #emph[particular] Sin, and doest not consider that thou art #emph[nothing] but Sin.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[Let me add this to them who are #emph[Preachers] of the #emph[Word,] or intend through the good hand of God that Employment. It is their Duty to plead with men about their Sins, to lay #emph[load] on particular sins, but always #emph[remember,] that it be done with that which is the proper End of Law and Gospel. That is, that they make use of the Sin they speak against, to the #emph[discovery] of the #emph[State] and #emph[Condition] wherein the #emph[Sinner] is. Otherwise, happily they may work men to #emph[Formality] and #emph[Hypocrisy,] but little of the true End of Preaching the #emph[Gospel] will be brought about. It will not #emph[avail,] to beat a man off from his #emph[Drunkenness,] into a #emph[sober Formality]\; A skillful Master of the #emph[Assemblies] lays his #emph[Axe] at the Root, drives still at the #emph[heart.] To inveigh against particular sins of ignorant #emph[unregenerate] persons, (such as the #emph[Land] is full of,) is a good Work: But yet though it may be done with great #emph[efficacy,] vigor and #emph[success,] if this be all the #emph[effect] of it, that they are set upon the most #emph[sedulous] Endeavors of #emph[mortifying] their sins preached down, all that is done, is but like the beating of an #emph[Enemy] in an #emph[open field,] and driving him into an #emph[impregnable] Castle, not to be prevailed against. Get you at any time a sinner at the advantage, on the account of any #emph[one] sin whatever, have you any thing to take hold of him by, bring it to his #emph[State] and #emph[Condition, drive it] up to the #emph[head,] and there deal with him; to break men off from particular sins, and not to break their Hearts, is to deprive ourselves of Advantages of dealing with them.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[And herein is the #emph[Roman Mortification] grievously #emph[peccant]\; they drive #emph[all sorts] of persons to it, without the least Consideration whether they have a #emph[principle] for it or no. Yea they are so far from calling on men to #emph[believe,] that they may be able to #emph[mortify their Lusts,] that they call men to #emph[Mortification] instead of #emph[Believing.] The truth is, they neither know what it is to #emph[believe,] nor what #emph[Mortification] itself intends. #emph[Faith] with them is but a general #emph[assent] to the Doctrine taught in their #emph[Church]: And #emph[Mortification] the betaking of a man by a #emph[Vow] to some certain Course of Life, wherein he #emph[denies] himself something of the use of the things of this World, not without a considerable Compensation. Such men know neither the #emph[Scriptures,] nor the #emph[Power] of God. Their boasting of their #emph[Mortification,] is but their #emph[Glorying] in their #emph[shame.] Some #emph[Casuists] among ourselves, who over-looking the Necessity of #emph[Regeneration,] do avowedly give this for a Direction to all sorts of persons, that complain of any Sin or Lust, that they should vow against it, at least for a season, a Month or so, seem to have a scantling of #emph[Light] in the #emph[Mystery] of the Gospel, much like that of #emph[Nicodemus,] when he came first to Christ. They bid men #emph[vow] to abstain from their #emph[sin] for a season. This commonly makes their #emph[lust] more impetuous. Perhaps with great #emph[perplexity] they keep their word: Perhaps not, which increases their Guilt and Torment. Is their sin at all #emph[mortified] hereby? Do they find a #emph[conquest] over it? Is their Condition changed, though they attain a Relinquishment of it? Are they not still in the #emph[Gall of bitterness]? Is not this to put men to make #emph[Brick,] if not without #emph[straw,] (which is worse,) without #emph[strength?] What Promise hath any #emph[unregenerate] man to countenance him in this work? What #emph[assistance] for the performance of it? Can sin be killed without an interest in the #emph[Death] of Christ, or #emph[Mortified] without the Spirit? If such Directions should prevail to #emph[change] men's #emph[Lives,] as seldom they do, yet they never reach to the #emph[change] of their #emph[hearts] or Conditions. They may make men #emph[self-justiciaries] or Hypocrites, not Christians. It grieves me oft-times to see poor Souls, that have a Zeal for God, and a desire of #emph[eternal Welfare,] kept, by such Directors and Directions, under an #emph[hard, burdensome, outside] Worship and Service of God, with many specious Endeavors for #emph[Mortification,] in an utter Ignorance of the #emph[Righteousness of Christ,] and unacquaintedness with his #emph[Spirit,] all their days. Persons and things of this kind, I know too many. If ever God #emph[shine into their hearts,] to give them the #emph[knowledge of his Glory in the face of his Son Jesus Christ,] they will see the #emph[folly] of their present way.]]
